.TH tapectl-catalog-search 1  "tapectl-catalog-search " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-catalog\-search \- Search for files by pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl catalog search\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATTERN\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search for files by pattern
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 50]
Limit results
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATTERN\fR>
Search pattern. Split on non\-alphanumerics; each token is PREFIX\-matched and all must match (AND). So "foo bar" finds paths containing a word starting with foo AND one starting with bar \-\- it is not a substring match, and "ar" will not find "bar"
